    s.append(" * =====================================================================================================================")
    s.append(" * CYBER-PHYSICAL WEB OFFSET DYNAMICS & MATHEMATICAL FORMULATIONS:")
    s.append(" * 1. Web Viscoelastic Strain Transport & Kelvin-Voigt Dynamic Modulus:")
    s.append(" *    Paper behaves as an anisotropic viscoelastic polymer composite whose Young's modulus E(T, M, eps_dot) decays")
    s.append(" *    exponentially with temperature and dampening moisture content, while stiffening at elevated web velocities (strain rates):")
    s.append(" *      E_eff(t) = E_0 * (1.0 - alpha_T * (T_web(t) - T_ref)) * (1.0 - beta_M * (M_web(t) - M_ref)) + eta_kv * (d_eps/dt)")
    s.append(" *    Along the continuous web path spanning infeed nip, 4 printing couples, HVHA dryer, chill rolls, and folder,")
    s.append(" *    the dynamic strain propagation across span length L_i at web velocity v_i satisfies the non-linear hyperbolic PDE:")
    s.append(" *      d(T_i)/dt = (v_i / L_i) * ( E_eff * A_cs * ((v_i - v_{i-1}) / v_{i-1}) + T_{i-1} - T_i )")
    s.append(" *    where A_cs = caliper * width is the cross-sectional web area. A sudden temperature jump in the 280 deg C dryer")
    s.append(" *    causes instantaneous flash-off of moisture (M_web dropping from 6.5% to 1.8%), triggering thermal shrinkage and")
    s.append(" *    elastic modulus transients that induce high-risk web breaks without active tension decoupling.")
    s.append(" *")
    s.append(" * 2. 4-Color (CMYK) Registration Decoupling & Hygroscopic Fan-Out Dynamic Model:")
    s.append(" *    Print registration is governed by two orthogonal error vectors: circumferential error (Delta y) and lateral error (Delta x).")
    s.append(" *    Circumferential error is coupled to servo cylinder phase trim Delta theta and inter-unit web tension T_web:")
    s.append(" *      Delta y_k = R_cylinder * Delta theta_k - Integral( (v_k - v_{k-1}) / v_0 ) * dt + (L_{span} / (E_eff * A_cs)) * Delta T")
    s.append(" *    Lateral error exhibits the classic 'fan-out' phenomenon, where the dampening water applied at the Cyan and Magenta units")
    s.append(" *    diffuses into the cellulose fiber matrix, causing cross-directional hygroscopic web expansion Delta W:")
    s.append(" *      Delta W_k = W_0 * alpha_hygro * (M_{web,k} - M_0)")
    s.append(" *    The dynamic decoupling matrix inverts this interaction to calculate simultaneous motorized plate cylinder axial")
    s.append(" *    cocking/traverse adjustments and circumferential harmonic phase corrections to hold Delta x, Delta y < 0.02 mm at 15.0 m/s.")
    s.append(" *")
    s.append(" * 3. Continuous Brush Dampening Hydrophilic Emulsion & Ink Tackiness Boundary Layer:")
    s.append(" *    Alcohol-free fountain solution utilizes non-ionic surfactants to lower dynamic surface tension gamma from 72.8 mN/m")
    s.append(" *    down to 35.0 mN/m. The water film thickness h_w transferred from the brush dampener roller to the hydrophilic plate is:")
    s.append(" *      h_w = k_brush * (omega_brush / omega_cylinder) * (mu_fountain / gamma_st)^0.5")
    s.append(" *    Water evaporation flux from the non-image plate areas into boundary layer air is governed by Dalton's mass transfer:")
    s.append(" *      m_dot_evap = (k_diff * M_h2o / (R_gas * T_surf)) * (P_sat(T_surf) - phi_rel * P_sat(T_amb))")
    s.append(" *    Simultaneously, water droplets emulsified into the lithographic ink alter the dynamic tackiness tau_tack:")
    s.append(" *      tau_tack = tau_0 * exp( -gamma_emuls * (V_water / (V_ink + V_water)) ) * (1.0 + c_shear * (omega_cyl / r_nip))")
    s.append(" *    Insufficient fountain solution results in ink scumming (plate background catch-up), while excessive water causes")
    s.append(" *    ink emulsification breakdown, roller stripping, and color density fade.")
    s.append(" *")
    s.append(" * 4. High-Velocity Hot Air (HVHA) Dryer Flue Gas & Lower Explosive Limit (LEL) Safety Observer:")
    s.append(" *    The 4-zone HVHA dryer impinges heated flue gas jets at 280 deg C and 35 m/s nozzle velocity onto both web faces.")
    s.append(" *    Heatset printing inks contain mineral oil distillates (C12-C16 hydrocarbons) that evaporate into the dryer atmosphere.")
    s.append(" *    The solvent evaporation rate m_dot_solv is coupled to web surface temperature T_web and heat transfer coefficient h_conv:")
    s.append(" *      m_dot_solv(z) = rho_ink * delta_film * v_web * (1.0 - exp(-k_evap * L_zone / v_web)) * f_evap(T_web(z))")
    s.append(" *    The dynamic solvent vapor mass balance inside dryer enclosure volume V_dryer with exhaust flow Q_exh and recirculation Q_rec is:")
    s.append(" *      V_dryer * d(C_solv)/dt = m_dot_solv - (Q_exh + Q_leak) * C_solv + Q_rec * C_rec")
    s.append(" *    NFPA 86 mandates that solvent concentration C_solv must remain strictly below 25% of the Lower Explosive Limit (LEL = 40.0 g/m3).")
    s.append(" *    The LEL observer continuously calculates C_solv and dynamically modulates fresh air purge dampers and burner modulation valves.")
    s.append(" *")
    s.append(" * 5. 4-Roll Chill Stand Web Condensation & Thermal Shock Conditioning:")
    s.append(" *    Hot printed web leaves the dryer at T_web = 135 deg C and traverses 4 counter-rotating chromium-plated chill rolls")
    s.append(" *    circulating chilled water at 12 deg C. Rapid thermal shock crystallizes the molten ink resins, freezing the pigment matrix:")
